; substring-one-meaning-band.fk — ONE MEANING FOR THE CUT, HELD BY FOUR ARMS.
;
; substring is the door the tree stands on: str_find, split-on, trim and char_at
; are recipes over it, and every frame reader, row walker and parser cuts through
; it. On 2026-09-07 a sibling made it native on fkwu and, measuring the edges,
; found that the four kernels did not agree on what a cut MEANS. Both halves of
; the divergence were silent.
;
; WHAT DIVERGED, measured on this tree the same day, `(substring "abcdefghij" a b)`:
;
;                        fkwu          go / rust / ts
;   (7, 2)  reversed     ""            DEAD  "bounds out of range start=7 end=2"
;   (0, 900) past end    "abcdefghij"  DEAD
;   (-6, 3) negative     "abc"         DEAD
;   (20, 25) past end    ""            DEAD
;   (42, 0, 2) non-str   ""            DEAD  "argStr: arg 0: expected str, got int"
;
;   and on "Ω+1", `(str_len (substring "Ω+1" a b))`:
;   (0, 1)               1             0     both ends floored to a char start
;   (1, 2)               1             2     floored down to 0, then whole Ω
;
; The second half is the quieter one. Flooring both offsets to character starts
; DOES keep the adjacency law among floored indices, which is what its comment
; claimed — but the body computes its indices in BYTES everywhere (str_byte_at is
; the narrow waist; the spool-and-bell transports, the <|ear:frame|> readers and
; the locale rows all count bytes), so on go, rust and ts those same indices
; silently yielded a shorter, shifted window. Every Persian, Hebrew, Chinese and
; Japanese row was exposed to it and no ASCII band could say so.
;
; THE ONE MEANING, and it is this body's own — core.fk's recipe and the fkwu
; native both said it from birth:
;
;   substring(s, start, end) answers the BYTES of s from max(start,0) up to
;   min(end, str_len(s)); the empty string when that range is empty or reversed;
;   the empty string when s is not a string. It refuses nothing and floors
;   nothing.
;
; WHERE AN ARM CANNOT SAY IT. fkwu's strings are raw byte buffers and Go's string
; is an arbitrary byte sequence, so those two hold every cut exactly. Rust's
; `str` carries a UTF-8 invariant and the TS kernel's string is UTF-16 whose
; str_len MEASURES its UTF-8 bytes; neither can hold a cut that severs a
; multi-byte character. Those two arms answer the axiom-1 absence there — the
; same choice rust's own read_file_slice already makes, "losslessness would need
; a byte string in the Value type" — rather than a plausible substitute. So the
; reading this band holds four ways is the one that covers both cases:
;
;   NO ARM EVER ANSWERS A DIFFERENT NON-EMPTY WINDOW.
;
; A severed cut is either the exact bytes or the absence; it is never the floored
; window, and it is never silently "". str_eq observes the absence on all four
; arms without dying, which is why every bit below is asked through str_eq.
;
; THIS BAND IS THE GUARD. It runs on all four kernels and it is a drift gate, so
; a kernel that drifts back to refusing or to flooring fails loudly and
; immediately rather than at the next multi-tongue row. ./validate.sh gates
; AGREEMENT, not correctness — three arms agreeing on a wrong cut would print
; green — so this band pins the meaning itself, against a reference it builds on
; the arm under test and against source literals the lexer carried.
;
; Verdict 4095 (12 bits):
;   1     every (start, end) in [-4, 14] x [-4, 14] over a ten-byte ASCII string
;         equals the clamped byte window this band builds from str_byte_at and
;         byte_to_str on the same arm — 361 cases, exhaustive
;   2     the clamping family named one by one: reversed, zero-length at every
;         position, start past the end, negative start, both negative, end far
;         past the end, and a billion
;   4     the five calls that killed go, rust and ts before today, asked against
;         literals written here rather than against bit 1's ruler
;   8     a non-string s and an empty s answer "" for every range asked
;   16    multi-byte cuts on character boundaries, against source literals:
;         Greek, Persian, Hebrew, Chinese, Japanese, and a four-byte emoji
;   32    byte width: str_len(substring(mt, 0, k)) is k at every character
;         boundary k of the multi-tongue literal — the property flooring breaks
;   64    the adjacency law at every character boundary of that literal
;   128   no floored counterfeit at any continuation byte of that literal: the
;         answer is neither the floored window nor ""
;   256   the real rows off disk, every byte offset that starts a character:
;         s[0:m] + s[m:n] is s
;   512   the real rows off disk, every continuation byte: no floored
;         counterfeit and no silent empty
;   1024  the whole file in one cut is the file, and its length is the file's
;   2048  the ruler is checked — this band's reference loop answers cases whose
;         answer is written in this source, so bit 1 is not a vacuous agreement
;
; PROOF LEVEL: FOUR-WAY — 4095 live on fkwu, go, rust and ts (2026-09-07). The
; three walkers answer it through form/validate.sh; the fourth arm is fkwu's own
; resolver-driven source door, run every land as a drift gate row
; (gate/drift-gates.bml, 4095 of 4095). It is NOT registered in
; fourth-arm-bands.txt: that manifest is the flatten lane, and we no longer
; flatten (Urs, 2026-08-27).
;
; Measured against a kernel carrying only the flooring half of the wound it
; answers 3455: bits 128 and 512 are exactly what separates a byte cut from a
; floored one, and bit 1 is what a refusing kernel dies on before it can reach
; them. A guard nobody has watched fail is a guard nobody has checked.
;
; Expected: 4095
;
; preludes: form-stdlib/core.fk

(do
    (defn sob-bit (ok bit) (if ok bit 0))
    (defn sob-and2 (a b) (if (and (eq a 1) (eq b 1)) 1 0))
    (defn sob-and3 (a b c) (sob-and2 a (sob-and2 b c)))
    (defn sob-and4 (a b c d) (sob-and2 (sob-and2 a b) (sob-and2 c d)))
    (defn sob-and5 (a b c d e) (sob-and2 (sob-and4 a b c d) e))
    (defn sob-and6 (a b c d e f) (sob-and2 (sob-and4 a b c d) (sob-and2 e f)))

    ; --- the ruler: the clamped byte window, built one byte at a time from the
    ; narrow waist on the arm under test. Sound for ASCII on all four arms:
    ; byte_to_str re-encodes above 127 on go/rust/ts (core.fk's byte-waist
    ; header), so this ruler is only ever laid against ASCII here.
    (defn sob-ref-go (s i end acc)
        (if (ge i end) acc
            (sob-ref-go s (add i 1) end (str_concat acc (byte_to_str (str_byte_at s i))))))
    (defn sob-ref (s a b)
        (do (let n (str_len s))
            (let lo (if (lt a 0) 0 a))
            (let hi (if (gt b n) n b))
            (if (le hi lo) "" (sob-ref-go s lo hi ""))))

    (defn sob-same? (s a b) (if (str_eq (substring s a b) (sob-ref s a b)) 1 0))
    (defn sob-is? (s a b want) (if (str_eq (substring s a b) want) 1 0))
    (defn sob-not? (s a b want) (if (str_eq (substring s a b) want) 0 1))

    ; --- bit 1: every start against every end, negatives and past-the-end included
    (defn sob-sweep-end (s a b hi)
        (if (gt b hi) 1
            (if (eq (sob-same? s a b) 1) (sob-sweep-end s a (add b 1) hi) 0)))
    (defn sob-sweep (s a hi lo)
        (if (gt a hi) 1
            (if (eq (sob-sweep-end s a lo hi) 1) (sob-sweep s (add a 1) hi lo) 0)))

    (defn sob-zero-at (s i n)
        (if (gt i n) 1
            (if (eq (sob-is? s i i "") 1) (sob-zero-at s (add i 1) n) 0)))

    ; --- the byte reading of a string, with no door but str_byte_at
    (defn sob-cont? (s i)
        (do (let b (str_byte_at s i))
            (if (and (ge b 128) (lt b 192)) 1 0)))
    (defn sob-floor (s i)
        (if (le i 0) 0 (if (eq (sob-cont? s i) 1) (sob-floor s (sub i 1)) i)))

    ; a severed cut is never the floored window and never a silent empty
    (defn sob-no-counterfeit (s i)
        (do (let f (sob-floor s i))
            (sob-and2
                (if (str_eq (substring s 0 i) (substring s 0 f)) 0 1)
                (if (str_eq (substring s 0 i) "") 0 1))))

    ; a character boundary keeps the adjacency law, byte for byte
    (defn sob-adjacent-at (s i n)
        (if (str_eq (str_concat (substring s 0 i) (substring s i n)) s) 1 0))

    ; --- the two walks over one string: boundaries only, and continuations only
    (defn sob-walk-bound (s i n)
        (if (ge i n) 1
            (if (eq (sob-cont? s i) 1) (sob-walk-bound s (add i 1) n)
                (if (eq (sob-adjacent-at s i n) 1) (sob-walk-bound s (add i 1) n) 0))))
    (defn sob-walk-cont (s i n)
        (if (ge i n) 1
            (if (eq (sob-cont? s i) 0) (sob-walk-cont s (add i 1) n)
                (if (eq (sob-no-counterfeit s i) 1) (sob-walk-cont s (add i 1) n) 0))))
    (defn sob-walk-width (s i n)
        (if (ge i n) 1
            (if (eq (sob-cont? s i) 1) (sob-walk-width s (add i 1) n)
                (if (eq (str_len (substring s 0 i)) i) (sob-walk-width s (add i 1) n) 0))))

    (defn substring-one-meaning-band ()
        (do
            (let h "abcdefghij")
            ; a is 1 byte, Ω 2, each Persian and Hebrew letter 2, each Chinese and
            ; Japanese 3, the emoji 4 — 43 bytes, measured on all four arms
            (let mt "aΩ|گفت|שלום|中文|日本語|😀|z")
            (let mn (str_len mt))
            (let rows (read_file "form/form-stdlib/locale-rows/symbol-words.rows"))
            (let rn (str_len rows))

            (sum (list
                (sob-bit (eq (sob-sweep h -4 14 -4) 1) 1)

                (sob-bit (eq (sob-and6
                    (sob-is? h 7 2 "")
                    (sob-zero-at h 0 10)
                    (sob-is? h 20 25 "")
                    (sob-is? h -6 3 "abc")
                    (sob-is? h -9 -2 "")
                    (sob-is? h 0 1000000000 "abcdefghij")) 1) 2)

                (sob-bit (eq (sob-and5
                    (sob-is? h 7 2 "")
                    (sob-is? h 0 900 "abcdefghij")
                    (sob-is? h -6 3 "abc")
                    (sob-is? h 20 25 "")
                    (sob-is? h 2 5 "cde")) 1) 4)

                (sob-bit (eq (sob-and4
                    (sob-is? 42 0 2 "")
                    (sob-is? 42 -3 900 "")
                    (sob-is? "" 0 5 "")
                    (sob-is? "" -2 2 "")) 1) 8)

                (sob-bit (eq (sob-and6
                    (sob-is? "aΩb" 0 3 "aΩ")
                    (sob-is? "گفت" 0 2 "گ")
                    (sob-is? "שלום" 0 2 "ש")
                    (sob-is? "中文" 0 3 "中")
                    (sob-is? "日本語" 3 6 "本")
                    (sob-is? "😀x" 0 4 "😀")) 1) 16)

                (sob-bit (eq (sob-and2
                    (sob-walk-width mt 0 mn)
                    (if (eq (str_len (substring mt 0 mn)) mn) 1 0)) 1) 32)

                (sob-bit (eq (sob-walk-bound mt 0 mn) 1) 64)

                (sob-bit (eq (sob-and3
                    (sob-walk-cont mt 0 mn)
                    (sob-not? "aΩb" 0 2 "a")
                    (sob-not? "aΩb" 0 2 "")) 1) 128)

                (sob-bit (eq (sob-walk-bound rows 0 rn) 1) 256)

                (sob-bit (eq (sob-walk-cont rows 0 rn) 1) 512)

                (sob-bit (eq (sob-and3
                    (if (str_eq (substring rows 0 rn) rows) 1 0)
                    (if (eq (str_len (substring rows 0 rn)) rn) 1 0)
                    (if (gt rn 400) 1 0)) 1) 1024)

                (sob-bit (eq (sob-and4
                    (if (str_eq (sob-ref h 2 5) "cde") 1 0)
                    (if (str_eq (sob-ref h -3 20) "abcdefghij") 1 0)
                    (if (str_eq (sob-ref h 7 2) "") 1 0)
                    (if (str_eq (sob-ref h 0 0) "") 1 0)) 1) 2048)))))

    (substring-one-meaning-band))
